Monster spells are made available based on monster level. A gnomish wizard
who has eaten a whole lot of wraith corpses or quaffed a big stack of
potions of gain level can cast the touch of death, summon nasties, &c.
However, you're unlikely to encounter such a foe unless someone has left
a particularly malicious bones file, and even high-level caster monsters
don't have anything that's really the equivalent of, say, magic missile.

Even on a run, it's true that I'm never really worried about gnomish
wizards taking me out with damage; I do think it would make them more
powerful to give them a greater chance of confusing or stunning the
player, though, as that's almost more dangerous than damage in the early
game, and in my opinion makes more sense. For one thing, this might tone
down the power of Elbereth a little bit...

